<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danube Swabians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Donauschwaben</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> Swabians are German-speaking people descended from settlers who moved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/backa">Bačka</a> and the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a>, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> reconquest from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the 18th century. Many came from south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, though not only from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a>. At the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> most fled or were expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, and many were interned or deported.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danube-swabians.jpg" alt="Danube Swabians" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Argean · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Danube_Swabians.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
